w("# SECTION 4: SWING GUI EXPLAINED")
w("===================================")
w("")
w("## Key Swing Concepts")
w("")
w("JFrame          : Top-level window. Every screen in this app is a JFrame subclass.")
w("JPanel          : Container for grouping components inside a frame.")
w("JTable          : Displays data in a grid of rows and columns.")
w("DefaultTableModel: Backing store for JTable data. addRow(), setRowCount(0) to clear.")
w("JScrollPane     : Wraps JTable to add scrollbars when data overflows.")
w("JTabbedPane     : Shows multiple panels one at a time, switching via tab labels.")
w("JSplitPane      : Splits an area into two resizable halves.")
w("JTextField      : Single-line text input box.")
w("JPasswordField  : Like JTextField but displays bullet characters.")
w("JTextArea       : Multi-line text area (used for revenue report output).")
w("JButton         : Clickable button.")
w("JLabel          : Non-editable text label.")
w("JOptionPane     : Pre-built popup dialogs (showMessageDialog, showConfirmDialog).")
w("")
w("ActionListener  : Interface with one method - actionPerformed(ActionEvent e).")
w("                  Wired to buttons: button.addActionListener(e -> method());")
w("                  Written as a lambda in this project.")
w("")
w("ListSelectionListener : Interface fired when user clicks a JTable row.")
w("                  table.getSelectionModel().addListSelectionListener(e -> method());")
w("")
w("Event Dispatch Thread (EDT):")
w("  Swing is single-threaded. All UI operations must run on the EDT.")
w("  SwingUtilities.invokeLater() schedules code to run on the EDT.")
w("")
w("    // Main.java - lines 14-18")
w("    SwingUtilities.invokeLater(() -> {")
w("        LoginFrame loginFrame = new LoginFrame();")
w("        loginFrame.setVisible(true);")
w("    });")
w("")
w("  In this project, DB calls also happen on the EDT (inside ActionListeners).")
w("  The UI freezes briefly during each DB query.")
w("  In production: use SwingWorker to run DB calls in a background thread.")
w("")
