w("# SECTION 5: JDBC EXPLAINED")
w("==============================")
w("")
w("## What is JDBC?")
w("")
w("JDBC (Java Database Connectivity) is the standard Java API for connecting to relational")
w("databases. You write SQL as strings in Java, send them to the database, and get results")
w("back as a ResultSet object. The MySQL Connector/J JAR (mysql-connector-j-9.2.0.jar)")
w("implements the JDBC interfaces for MySQL.")
w("")
w("Key JDBC interfaces and classes used in this project:")
w("  java.sql.Connection         : Represents a connection to MySQL.")
w("  java.sql.PreparedStatement  : Pre-compiled SQL with ? placeholders.")
w("  java.sql.CallableStatement  : For calling stored procedures.")
w("  java.sql.ResultSet          : Cursor over rows returned by a SELECT.")
w("  java.sql.DriverManager      : Factory that creates Connection objects.")
w("  java.sql.Statement          : Used only for RETURN_GENERATED_KEYS constant.")
w("  java.sql.Timestamp          : Converts Java LocalDateTime to SQL DATETIME.")
w("")
w("---")
w("")
w("## Step 1: Getting a Connection")
w("")
w("    // util/AppConfig.java - lines 3-18")
w("    public static String getDbUrl() {")
w("        return System.getenv().getOrDefault(")
w('            "DB_URL",')
w('            "jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/ev_charging_system?useSSL=false&serverTimezone=Asia/Kolkata"')
w("        );")
w("    }")
w("    public static String getDbUser() {")
w('        return System.getenv().getOrDefault("DB_USER", "root");')
w("    }")
w("    public static String getDbPassword() {")
w('        return System.getenv().getOrDefault("DB_PASSWORD", "");')
w("    }")
w("")
w("    // util/DBConnection.java - lines 7-23")
w("    static {")
w('        Class.forName("com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver");  // registers the MySQL driver')
w("    }")
w("")
w("    public static Connection getConnection() throws SQLException {")
w("        return DriverManager.getConnection(")
w("            AppConfig.getDbUrl(), AppConfig.getDbUser(), AppConfig.getDbPassword()")
w("        );")
w("    }")
w("")
w("JDBC URL format:")
w("  jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/ev_charging_system?useSSL=false&serverTimezone=Asia/Kolkata")
w("  |___|mysql|__|___________||__________________|")
w("  protocol  host  port     database name")
w("")
w("DriverManager.getConnection() opens a new TCP connection to MySQL each call.")
w("There is NO connection pool - each DAO method opens and closes its own connection.")
w("This is fine for a small university project; in production, use HikariCP or c3p0.")
w("")
w("---")
w("")
w("## Step 2: PreparedStatement - What it is and why it is used")
w("")
w("A PreparedStatement is a pre-compiled SQL template.")
w("? marks are placeholders for values that are set with setXxx() methods.")
w("")
w("Example:")
w('    String sql = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ?";')
w("    PreparedStatement stmt = conn.prepareStatement(sql);")
w("    stmt.setString(1, email);  // sets the first ? to the email value")
w("    ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery();")
w("")
w("Why NOT use String concatenation like this:")
w('    String sql = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = \'" + email + "\'";  // DANGEROUS!')
w("")
w("Reason 1 - SQL Injection Prevention:")
w("  If the user types  ' OR '1'='1  in the email field, the concatenated SQL becomes:")
w("    SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = '' OR '1'='1'")
w("  This returns ALL users! An attacker could log in as anyone.")
w("  With PreparedStatement, that input is treated as a literal string value,")
w("  not as SQL syntax. The query would look for an email that literally equals")
w("    ' OR '1'='1  and find no results. Safe.")
w("")
w("Reason 2 - Type Safety:")
w("  setLong(1, userId) ensures the value is passed as a numeric type,")
w("  not as a string that the DB has to parse.")
w("")
w("Reason 3 - Code Clarity:")
w("  SQL logic is separated from the data values, making code easier to read.")
w("")
w("    // dao/UserDAO.java - lines 13-25")
w('    String sql = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = ?";')
w("    try (Connection conn = DBConnection.getConnection();")
w("         PreparedStatement stmt = conn.prepareStatement(sql)) {")
w("        stmt.setString(1, email);")
w("        try (ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery()) {")
w("            if (rs.next()) {")
w("                return Optional.of(mapResultSetToUser(rs));")
w("            }")
w("        }")
w("    }")
w("")
w("Note the try-with-resources pattern: try (Connection conn = ...; PreparedStatement stmt = ...)")
w("This ensures conn.close() and stmt.close() are called automatically,")
w("even if an exception occurs. This prevents connection leaks.")
w("")
w("---")
w("")
w("## Step 3: Mapping ResultSet to Model Objects")
w("")
w("A ResultSet is a cursor pointing to rows returned by a SELECT.")
w("rs.next() advances the cursor. Read each column by name using getXxx(columnName).")
w("")
w("    // dao/UserDAO.java - lines 50-62")
w("    private User mapResultSetToUser(ResultSet rs) throws SQLException {")
w("        return new User(")
w('            rs.getLong("user_id"),')
w('            rs.getString("first_name"),')
w('            rs.getString("last_name"),')
w('            rs.getString("email"),')
w('            rs.getString("phone"),')
w('            rs.getString("password_hash"),')
w('            UserRole.valueOf(rs.getString("role")),      // "CUSTOMER" -> UserRole.CUSTOMER')
w('            UserStatus.valueOf(rs.getString("status")),  // "ACTIVE"   -> UserStatus.ACTIVE')
w('            rs.getTimestamp("created_at").toLocalDateTime()')
w("        );")
w("    }")
w("")
w("The same pattern is in SlotDAO.mapResultSetToSlot(), StationDAO.mapResultSetToStation(),")
w("and PaymentDAO.mapResultSetToPayment().")
w("")
w("---")
w("")
w("## Step 4: Transactions (setAutoCommit, commit, rollback)")
w("")
w("By default, JDBC auto-commits every SQL statement immediately.")
w("For the booking flow, we need 4 SQL statements to all succeed together,")
w("or all be undone (rolled back) together. This is an ACID transaction.")
w("")
w("ACID:")
w("  Atomicity   : All 4 statements succeed or all are undone.")
w("  Consistency : DB goes from one valid state to another.")
w("  Isolation   : Other transactions cannot see partial results of this transaction.")
w("  Durability  : Once committed, the data persists even if the server crashes.")
w("")
w("    // dao/BookingDAO.java - lines 28-100")
w("    Connection conn = null;")
w("    try {")
w("        conn = DBConnection.getConnection();")
w("        conn.setAutoCommit(false);   // START TRANSACTION")
w("")
w("        // Step 1: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE  (lock slot row)")
w("        // Step 2: SELECT ... FOR UPDATE  (check overlap, lock conflicting rows)")
w("        // Step 3: INSERT INTO bookings")
w("        // Step 4: INSERT INTO payments")
w("")
w("        conn.commit();   // COMMIT - make all 4 changes permanent")
w("        return bookingId;")
w("")
w("    } catch (SQLException e) {")
w("        if (conn != null) conn.rollback();  // ROLLBACK - undo all changes")
w("        throw e;")
w("    } finally {")
w("        if (conn != null) {")
w("            conn.setAutoCommit(true);  // restore default")
w("            conn.close();")
w("        }")
w("    }")
w("")
w("Isolation Level:")
w("  Default MySQL InnoDB isolation level = REPEATABLE READ.")
w("  FOR UPDATE upgrades selected rows to exclusive write locks.")
w("  No other transaction can UPDATE or lock those rows until this transaction commits.")
w("")
w("---")
w("")
w("## Step 5: Calling a Stored Procedure (CallableStatement)")
w("")
w("    // service/AdminService.java - lines 65-89")
w('    String sql = "{CALL sp_station_revenue(?, ?, ?)}";  // JDBC escape syntax')
w("")
w("    try (Connection conn = DBConnection.getConnection();")
w("         CallableStatement stmt = conn.prepareCall(sql)) {")
w("")
w("        stmt.setLong(1, stationId);")
w("        stmt.setTimestamp(2, Timestamp.valueOf(fromDate));")
w("        stmt.setTimestamp(3, Timestamp.valueOf(toDate));")
w("")
w("        try (ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery()) {")
w("            if (rs.next()) {")
w('                report.put("station_id",          rs.getLong("station_id"));')
w('                report.put("station_name",         rs.getString("station_name"));')
w('                report.put("paid_bookings_count",  rs.getInt("paid_bookings_count"));')
w('                report.put("total_paid_revenue",   rs.getBigDecimal("total_paid_revenue"));')
w('                report.put("total_refunded_amount",rs.getBigDecimal("total_refunded_amount"));')
w('                report.put("net_revenue",          rs.getBigDecimal("net_revenue"));')
w("            }")
w("        }")
w("    }")
w("    return report;  // Map<String, Object>")
w("")
w("CallableStatement is the JDBC class for stored procedures.")
w("{CALL proc_name(?, ?, ?)} is the JDBC-standard portable escape syntax.")
w("The procedure returns a ResultSet, read the same way as any SELECT.")
w("Timestamp.valueOf(localDateTime) converts Java LocalDateTime to java.sql.Timestamp")
w("which JDBC maps to MySQL DATETIME.")
w("")
w("---")
w("")
w("## Step 6: Getting Generated Keys (AUTO_INCREMENT IDs)")
w("")
w("After an INSERT, you often need the auto-generated primary key (user_id, slot_id, etc.):")
w("")
w("    // dao/UserDAO.java - lines 27-47")
w("    PreparedStatement stmt = conn.prepareStatement(sql, Statement.RETURN_GENERATED_KEYS);")
w("    stmt.executeUpdate();")
w("    try (ResultSet rs = stmt.getGeneratedKeys()) {")
w("        if (rs.next()) {")
w("            user.setUserId(rs.getLong(1));  // column 1 = the generated user_id")
w("        }")
w("    }")
w("")
w("Statement.RETURN_GENERATED_KEYS is a flag telling JDBC to capture the auto-increment value.")
w("stmt.getGeneratedKeys() returns a ResultSet with one row and one column: the new ID.")
w("")
w("This pattern is used in:")
w("  UserDAO.createUser() -> sets user.userId")
w("  SlotDAO.createSlot() -> sets slot.slotId")
w("  StationDAO.createStation() -> sets station.stationId")
w("  BookingDAO.bookSlotTransactional() -> captures bookingId, then uses it for the payment INSERT")
w("")
w("---")
w("")
w("# SECTION 6: DATABASE EXPLAINED")
w("==================================")
w("")
w("All SQL is in dbcode.txt. Database name: ev_charging_system. Engine: InnoDB.")
w("InnoDB is required for foreign keys and transactions (MyISAM does not support these).")
w("")
w("The schema has 5 tables:")
w("  users -> ev_stations -> charging_slots -> bookings -> payments")
w("")
w("---")
w("")
w("## Table 1: users")
w("")
w("Purpose: Stores every person who can log in - both customers and the admin.")
w("")
w("    -- dbcode.txt lines 4-14")
w("    CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (")
w("        user_id       BIGINT UNSIGNED AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,")
w("        first_name    VARCHAR(50)  NOT NULL,")
w("        last_name     VARCHAR(50)  NOT NULL,")
w("        email         VARCHAR(120) NOT NULL UNIQUE,")
w("        phone         VARCHAR(20)  NOT NULL UNIQUE,")
w("        password_hash VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,")
w("        role          ENUM('CUSTOMER','ADMIN') NOT NULL DEFAULT 'CUSTOMER',")
w("        status        ENUM('ACTIVE','BLOCKED')  NOT NULL DEFAULT 'ACTIVE',")
w("        created_at    TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP")
w("    ) ENGINE=InnoDB;")
w("")
w("Column by column:")
w("")
w("  user_id       : BIGINT UNSIGNED, PK, AUTO_INCREMENT")
w("                  Surrogate key. No natural key chosen as PK.")
w("  first_name    : VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL. Max 50 chars, cannot be empty.")
w("  last_name     : VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL.")
w("  email         : VARCHAR(120) NOT NULL UNIQUE.")
w("                  The unique constraint prevents two accounts with the same email.")
w("                  This is the login identifier checked in UserDAO.findByEmail().")
w("  phone         : VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL UNIQUE.")
w("                  UNIQUE prevents phone number reuse across accounts.")
w("  password_hash : VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL.")
w("                  Stores the PBKDF2 hash, never the plain password.")
w("                  Format: pbkdf2_sha256$600000$<salt_base64>$<hash_base64>")
w("  role          : ENUM('CUSTOMER','ADMIN') NOT NULL DEFAULT 'CUSTOMER'")
w("                  MySQL ENUM enforces that only these two values can be stored.")
w("                  Default is CUSTOMER, so new registrations don't need to set it.")
w("  status        : ENUM('ACTIVE','BLOCKED') NOT NULL DEFAULT 'ACTIVE'")
w("                  BLOCKED users are rejected at login in AuthService.login().")
w("  created_at    : TIMESTAMP NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP")
w("                  Auto-set by MySQL on INSERT. Java never writes this column.")
w("")
w("Normalization:")
w("  1NF: No repeating groups. Each cell holds one atomic value.")
w("  2NF: No partial dependencies (table has a single-column PK, so 2NF is automatic).")
w("  3NF: Every non-key column (first_name, email, role, etc.) depends directly")
w("       on user_id and on nothing else. No transitive dependencies.")
w("")
w("---")
w("")
w("## Table 2: ev_stations")
w("")
w("Purpose: Represents a physical EV charging station location.")
w("")
w("    -- dbcode.txt lines 16-32")
w("    CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS ev_stations (")
w("        station_id   BIGINT UNSIGNED AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,")
w("        station_name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,")
w("        address      VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,")
w("        city         VARCHAR(80)  NOT NULL,")
w("        state        VARCHAR(80)  NOT NULL,")
w("        postal_code  VARCHAR(15)  NOT NULL,")
w("        latitude     DECIMAL(9,6) NULL,")
w("        longitude    DECIMAL(9,6) NULL,")
w("        opening_time TIME         NOT NULL,")
w("        closing_time TIME         NOT NULL,")
w("        status       ENUM('ACTIVE','MAINTENANCE','INACTIVE') NOT NULL DEFAULT 'ACTIVE',")
w("        created_at   TIMESTAMP    NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,")
w("        CONSTRAINT chk_station_hours CHECK (opening_time < closing_time),")
w("        CONSTRAINT chk_station_lat   CHECK (latitude  IS NULL OR (latitude  BETWEEN -90  AND 90)),")
w("        CONSTRAINT chk_station_lon   CHECK (longitude IS NULL OR (longitude BETWEEN -180 AND 180))")
w("    ) ENGINE=InnoDB;")
w("")
w("Column notes:")
w("")
w("  latitude / longitude : DECIMAL(9,6)")
w("                  9 total digits, 6 after the decimal point.")
w("                  Example: 18.520400 (Pune, Maharashtra)")
w("                  NULL allowed for stations that don't have GPS coordinates yet.")
w("  opening_time / closing_time : TIME type (HH:MM:SS).")
w("  status        : ACTIVE = bookable. MAINTENANCE = temporarily offline.")
w("                  INACTIVE = permanently removed. Customers see only ACTIVE stations.")
w("")
w("CHECK Constraints:")
w("  chk_station_hours : opening_time < closing_time")
w("                      Cannot create a station that closes before it opens.")
w("  chk_station_lat   : latitude must be NULL or between -90 and 90.")
w("  chk_station_lon   : longitude must be NULL or between -180 and 180.")
w("  If you try to INSERT a row that violates a CHECK constraint, MySQL rejects it.")
w("")
w("Normalization: All columns describe the station directly. No repeating groups. 3NF.")
w("")
w("---")
w("")
w("## Table 3: charging_slots")
w("")
w("Purpose: Each individual charging plug/point within a station. A station has many slots.")
w("")
w("    -- dbcode.txt lines 34-50")
w("    CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS charging_slots (")
w("        slot_id        BIGINT UNSIGNED AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,")
w("        station_id     BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,")
w("        slot_number    INT UNSIGNED    NOT NULL,")
w("        connector_type ENUM('CCS2','CHAdeMO','TYPE2','GB_T') NOT NULL,")
w("        max_power_kw   DECIMAL(6,2)   NOT NULL,")
w("        hourly_rate    DECIMAL(10,2)  NOT NULL,")
w("        status         ENUM('ACTIVE','MAINTENANCE','INACTIVE') NOT NULL DEFAULT 'ACTIVE',")
w("        created_at     TIMESTAMP      NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,")
w("        CONSTRAINT fk_slot_station")
w("            FOREIGN KEY (station_id) REFERENCES ev_stations(station_id)")
w("            ON UPDATE CASCADE ON DELETE RESTRICT,")
w("        CONSTRAINT uq_slot_number UNIQUE (station_id, slot_number),")
w("        CONSTRAINT chk_slot_power CHECK (max_power_kw > 0),")
w("        CONSTRAINT chk_slot_rate  CHECK (hourly_rate >= 0)")
w("    ) ENGINE=InnoDB;")
w("")
w("Column notes:")
w("")
w("  station_id     : FK -> ev_stations(station_id)")
w("                   ON DELETE RESTRICT: cannot delete a station that still has slots.")
w("                   ON UPDATE CASCADE: if station_id changes, cascades here automatically.")
w("  connector_type : ENUM with real EV charging standards.")
w("                   CCS2    = Combined Charging System 2. Most common in Europe and India.")
w("                   CHAdeMO = Japanese DC fast charging standard.")
w("                   TYPE2   = IEC 62196-2 AC charging standard.")
w("                   GB_T    = Chinese national standard (GB/T 20234).")
w("  max_power_kw   : DECIMAL(6,2). E.g. 60.00 = fast charger. 22.00 = medium AC charger.")
w("  hourly_rate    : DECIMAL(10,2). Price in Indian Rupees per hour.")
w("  UNIQUE (station_id, slot_number) : Composite unique key.")
w("                   Prevents having two 'Slot 1' at the same station.")
w("  chk_slot_power : max_power_kw > 0 (cannot have a zero-watt charger).")
w("  chk_slot_rate  : hourly_rate >= 0 (rate can be zero but not negative).")
w("")
w("Relationship: ev_stations -> charging_slots is 1:N")
w("  (One station has many slots; each slot belongs to exactly one station.)")
w("")
w("---")
w("")
w("## Table 4: bookings")
w("")
w("Purpose: Records every booking made by a customer for a specific slot at a specific time.")
w("")
w("    -- dbcode.txt lines 52-77")
w("    CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bookings (")
w("        booking_id      BIGINT UNSIGNED AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,")
w("        user_id         BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,")
w("        slot_id         BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL,")
w("        start_time      DATETIME(3)    NOT NULL,")
w("        end_time        DATETIME(3)    NOT NULL,")
w("        rate_per_hour   DECIMAL(10,2)  NOT NULL,")
w("        status          ENUM('CONFIRMED','CANCELLED','COMPLETED') NOT NULL DEFAULT 'CONFIRMED',")
w("        active_start_time DATETIME(3)")
w("            GENERATED ALWAYS AS (")
w("                CASE WHEN status = 'CONFIRMED' THEN start_time ELSE NULL END")
w("            ) STORED,")
w("        created_at      TIMESTAMP      NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,")
w("        updated_at      TIMESTAMP      NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,")
w("        CONSTRAINT fk_booking_user FOREIGN KEY (user_id) REFERENCES users(user_id)")
w("            ON UPDATE CASCADE ON DELETE RESTRICT,")
w("        CONSTRAINT fk_booking_slot FOREIGN KEY (slot_id) REFERENCES charging_slots(slot_id)")
w("            ON UPDATE CASCADE ON DELETE RESTRICT,")
w("        CONSTRAINT uq_active_slot_start UNIQUE (slot_id, active_start_time),")
w("        CONSTRAINT chk_booking_time CHECK (end_time > start_time),")
w("        CONSTRAINT chk_booking_rate CHECK (rate_per_hour >= 0)")
w("    ) ENGINE=InnoDB;")
w("")
w("Column notes:")
w("")
w("  start_time / end_time : DATETIME(3) = datetime with millisecond precision.")
w("                  The app always inserts these exactly 1 hour apart.")
w("                  (endTime = startTime.plusHours(1) in BookingDAO)")
w("")
w("  rate_per_hour : Copied from charging_slots.hourly_rate at the time of booking.")
w("                  This is a price snapshot. If the admin later changes the slot rate,")
w("                  old bookings still show the original price. Historically accurate.")
w("")
w("  active_start_time : GENERATED COLUMN (also called a computed column).")
w("                  MySQL computes this automatically - Java never inserts it.")
w("                  STORED means MySQL physically stores the value in the row.")
w("                  Value:")
w("                    = start_time   when status = 'CONFIRMED'")
w("                    = NULL         when status = 'CANCELLED' or 'COMPLETED'")
w("")
w("  UNIQUE (slot_id, active_start_time) : This unique constraint is the key to")
w("                  preventing double-booking at the database level.")
w("                  CONFIRMED booking: active_start_time = real datetime.")
w("                    -> Two CONFIRMED bookings for the same slot at the same time")
w("                       would have the same (slot_id, active_start_time) pair -> REJECTED.")
w("                  CANCELLED/COMPLETED: active_start_time = NULL.")
w("                    -> NULL != NULL in SQL unique checks (NULL is not equal to anything).")
w("                    -> So cancelled bookings do NOT block the unique constraint.")
w("                    -> You CAN re-book a time slot that was previously cancelled.")
w("")
w("  updated_at : TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP.")
w("               MySQL automatically updates this column whenever the row is modified.")
w("               The trigger's refunded payment sets payments.updated_at the same way.")
w("")
w("Relationships:")
w("  users -> bookings : 1:N (one user makes many bookings)")
w("  charging_slots -> bookings : 1:N (one slot can have many bookings at different times)")
w("")
w("Normalization note:")
w("  rate_per_hour appears to be redundant since charging_slots has hourly_rate.")
w("  But it is deliberately copied here as a historical price snapshot.")
w("  This is a conscious and justified denormalization - not a normalization violation.")
w("")
w("---")
w("")
w("## Table 5: payments")
w("")
w("Purpose: Stores the payment record for each booking. One booking has exactly one payment.")
w("")
w("    -- dbcode.txt lines 79-93")
w("    CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS payments (")
w("        payment_id            BIGINT UNSIGNED AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,")
w("        booking_id            BIGINT UNSIGNED NOT NULL UNIQUE,")
w("        amount                DECIMAL(10,2)  NOT NULL,")
w("        method                ENUM('MOCK')   NOT NULL DEFAULT 'MOCK',")
w("        status                ENUM('PAID','REFUNDED') NOT NULL DEFAULT 'PAID',")
w("        transaction_reference VARCHAR(80)    NOT NULL UNIQUE,")
w("        paid_at               TIMESTAMP      NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,")
w("        updated_at            TIMESTAMP      NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP ON UPDATE CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,")
w("        CONSTRAINT fk_payment_booking")
w("            FOREIGN KEY (booking_id) REFERENCES bookings(booking_id)")
w("            ON UPDATE CASCADE ON DELETE RESTRICT,")
w("        CONSTRAINT chk_payment_amount CHECK (amount >= 0)")
w("    ) ENGINE=InnoDB;")
w("")
w("Column notes:")
w("")
w("  booking_id            : FK -> bookings(booking_id). Also UNIQUE.")
w("                          The UNIQUE constraint enforces the 1:1 relationship at DB level.")
w("                          You cannot insert two payment rows for the same booking_id.")
w("  method                : ENUM('MOCK') only. No real payment gateway is integrated.")
w("  status                : PAID = money collected. REFUNDED = money returned.")
w("                          Changed from PAID to REFUNDED by trigger trg_booking_cancel_payment")
w("                          when the corresponding booking is cancelled.")
w("  transaction_reference : Generated in Java as 'TXN_MOCK_' + UUID substring.")
w("                          UNIQUE prevents accidental duplicate references.")
w("  paid_at               : Set by MySQL to CURRENT_TIMESTAMP on INSERT.")
w("  updated_at            : Updated automatically on UPDATE (e.g. when trigger runs).")
w("")
w("Relationship: bookings -> payments is 1:1")
w("  (each booking has exactly one payment record, enforced by UNIQUE on booking_id).")
w("")
w("---")
w("")
w("## Indexes")
w("")
w("    -- dbcode.txt lines 95-98")
w("    CREATE INDEX idx_slots_station_status      ON charging_slots(station_id, status);")
w("    CREATE INDEX idx_bookings_slot_time_status ON bookings(slot_id, start_time, end_time, status);")
w("    CREATE INDEX idx_bookings_user_time        ON bookings(user_id, start_time);")
w("    CREATE INDEX idx_payments_status_date      ON payments(status, paid_at);")
w("")
w("Explanation:")
w("")
w("  idx_slots_station_status")
w("    : Covers the query: SELECT * FROM charging_slots WHERE station_id = ? AND status = ?")
w("      Used by SlotDAO.findByStation() and the overlap check in BookingDAO.")
w("")
w("  idx_bookings_slot_time_status")
w("    : Covers the overlap check query:")
w("        WHERE slot_id = ? AND status = 'CONFIRMED'")
w("        AND start_time < ? AND end_time > ?")
w("      Without this index, MySQL would do a full scan of the bookings table for each booking attempt.")
w("")
w("  idx_bookings_user_time")
w("    : Covers: WHERE b.user_id = ? ORDER BY b.start_time DESC")
w("      Used by CustomerDashboardFrame.loadBookingHistory().")
w("")
w("  idx_payments_status_date")
w("    : Covers: WHERE status = ? AND paid_at BETWEEN ? AND ?")
w("      Used by sp_station_revenue JOIN condition on payments.")
w("")
w("---")
w("")
w("## Stored Function: fn_booking_hours")
w("")
w("    -- dbcode.txt lines 162-175")
w("    CREATE FUNCTION fn_booking_hours(p_start DATETIME, p_end DATETIME)")
w("    RETURNS DECIMAL(5,2)")
w("    DETERMINISTIC")
w("    BEGIN")
w("        DECLARE v_minutes INT;")
w("        IF p_start IS NULL OR p_end IS NULL OR p_end <= p_start THEN")
w("            RETURN 0.00;")
w("        END IF;")
w("        SET v_minutes = TIMESTAMPDIFF(MINUTE, p_start, p_end);")
w("        RETURN ROUND(v_minutes / 60.0, 2);")
w("    END")
w("")
w("Line-by-line:")
w("  RETURNS DECIMAL(5,2) : Return type declared before the body.")
w("  DETERMINISTIC        : Same inputs -> same output always.")
w("                         Required for binary logging and query optimization.")
w("  DECLARE v_minutes INT: Declares a local variable.")
w("  IF p_end <= p_start THEN RETURN 0.00 : Guard clause for invalid input.")
w("  TIMESTAMPDIFF(MINUTE, p_start, p_end) : MySQL built-in that computes difference in minutes.")
w("  ROUND(v_minutes / 60.0, 2) : Converts minutes to hours, rounds to 2 decimal places.")
w("")
w("Example: fn_booking_hours('2026-10-01 10:00:00', '2026-10-01 11:30:00') -> 1.50")
w("")
w("Is it called from Java? NO.")
w("The function is defined in dbcode.txt but no Java code calls fn_booking_hours().")
w("It demonstrates knowledge of stored functions but is not used by the running application.")
w("")
w("---")
w("")
w("## Stored Procedure: sp_station_revenue")
w("")
w("    -- dbcode.txt lines 177-203")
w("    CREATE PROCEDURE sp_station_revenue(")
w("        IN p_station_id BIGINT UNSIGNED,")
w("        IN p_from_date  DATETIME,")
w("        IN p_to_date    DATETIME")
w("    )")
w("    BEGIN")
w("        SELECT")
w("            es.station_id,")
w("            es.station_name,")
w("            COUNT(CASE WHEN p.status = 'PAID' THEN 1 END)     AS paid_bookings_count,")
w("            COALESCE(SUM(CASE WHEN p.status = 'PAID'")
w("                              THEN p.amount ELSE 0 END), 0.00) AS total_paid_revenue,")
w("            COALESCE(SUM(CASE WHEN p.status = 'REFUNDED'")
w("                              THEN p.amount ELSE 0 END), 0.00) AS total_refunded_amount,")
w("            COALESCE(")
w("                SUM(CASE WHEN p.status = 'PAID'     THEN p.amount ELSE 0 END) -")
w("                SUM(CASE WHEN p.status = 'REFUNDED' THEN p.amount ELSE 0 END),")
w("                0.00")
w("            ) AS net_revenue")
w("        FROM ev_stations es")
w("        LEFT JOIN charging_slots cs ON cs.station_id = es.station_id")
w("        LEFT JOIN bookings b        ON b.slot_id = cs.slot_id")
w("        LEFT JOIN payments p        ON p.booking_id = b.booking_id")
w("                  AND p.paid_at BETWEEN p_from_date AND p_to_date")
w("        WHERE es.station_id = p_station_id")
w("        GROUP BY es.station_id, es.station_name;")
w("    END")
w("")
w("Line-by-line explanation:")
w("")
w("  IN p_station_id, p_from_date, p_to_date")
w("    : Three input parameters passed from Java via CallableStatement.")
w("      IN means input-only; the procedure cannot change these values in the caller.")
w("")
w("  LEFT JOIN ev_stations -> charging_slots -> bookings -> payments")
w("    : Chains all 4 tables. LEFT JOIN is used so the station row appears")
w("      even if it has no charging slots, no bookings, or no payments.")
w("      With INNER JOIN, a station with no bookings would be excluded from results.")
w("")
w("  COUNT(CASE WHEN p.status = 'PAID' THEN 1 END)")
w("    : Conditional COUNT. CASE WHEN returns 1 for PAID rows and NULL for others.")
w("      COUNT ignores NULLs, so this effectively counts only PAID payments.")
w("")
w("  SUM(CASE WHEN p.status = 'PAID' THEN p.amount ELSE 0 END)")
w("    : Conditional SUM. Adds only the amounts for PAID status rows.")
w("      ELSE 0 means non-PAID rows contribute 0 to the sum.")
w("")
w("  COALESCE(..., 0.00)")
w("    : Returns 0.00 if the inner expression evaluates to NULL.")
w("      This happens when a station has no payments at all (all are NULL from the LEFT JOIN).")
w("")
w("  net_revenue = total_paid - total_refunded")
w("    : The business definition of net revenue (gross revenue minus refunds).")
w("")
w("  p.paid_at BETWEEN p_from_date AND p_to_date")
w("    : This filter is on the JOIN condition (not in the WHERE clause).")
w("      This is intentional: it means the station row is included even if no payments")
w("      fall in the date range - those columns just show 0. If this were in WHERE,")
w("      stations with no in-range payments would be excluded from the results entirely.")
w("")
w("  GROUP BY es.station_id, es.station_name")
w("    : Aggregates all rows (one per booking/payment) into a single summary row")
w("      per station.")
w("")
w("SQL concepts demonstrated:")
w("  LEFT JOIN, conditional COUNT, conditional SUM, COALESCE,")
w("  GROUP BY, BETWEEN, date range filter, 4-table join.")
w("")
w("How Java calls it:")
w('  AdminService.getStationRevenueReport() uses: "{CALL sp_station_revenue(?, ?, ?)}"')
w("  via a CallableStatement. The result is read into a Map<String, Object>.")
w("")
w("---")
w("")
w("## Trigger: trg_booking_cancel_payment")
w("")
w("    -- dbcode.txt lines 206-219")
w("    CREATE TRIGGER trg_booking_cancel_payment")
w("    AFTER UPDATE ON bookings")
w("    FOR EACH ROW")
w("    BEGIN")
w("        IF NEW.status = 'CANCELLED' AND OLD.status = 'CONFIRMED' THEN")
w("            UPDATE payments")
w("            SET status = 'REFUNDED',")
w("                updated_at = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP")
w("            WHERE booking_id = NEW.booking_id")
w("              AND status = 'PAID';")
w("        END IF;")
w("    END;")
w("")
w("Line-by-line explanation:")
w("")
w("  AFTER UPDATE ON bookings")
w("    : The trigger fires AFTER an UPDATE statement changes a row in bookings.")
w("      AFTER means the booking row is already updated when the trigger runs.")
w("      (BEFORE triggers fire before the change; AFTER fires after.)")
w("")
w("  FOR EACH ROW")
w("    : Row-level trigger. Fires once per updated row.")
w("      If one UPDATE statement changes 5 rows, the trigger fires 5 times.")
w("      (Statement-level triggers fire once per SQL statement regardless of rows.)")
w("")
w("  NEW.status")
w("    : The value of the status column AFTER the UPDATE.")
w("  OLD.status")
w("    : The value of the status column BEFORE the UPDATE.")
w("")
w("  IF NEW.status = 'CANCELLED' AND OLD.status = 'CONFIRMED'")
w("    : The trigger only acts when a booking transitions CONFIRMED -> CANCELLED.")
w("      This prevents it from firing when:")
w("        - A booking changes from CONFIRMED -> COMPLETED (e.g. end of session).")
w("        - Other columns on the row are updated.")
w("        - A booking changes from CANCELLED -> anything.")
w("")
w("  UPDATE payments SET status = 'REFUNDED'")
w("    : Marks the payment for this booking as refunded.")
w("      AND status = 'PAID' ensures we only refund payments that were PAID,")
w("      not payments already REFUNDED.")
w("")
w("How it is triggered from Java:")
w("  CustomerDashboardFrame.handleCancelBooking() sends this SQL:")
w("    UPDATE bookings SET status = 'CANCELLED' WHERE booking_id = ?")
w("  MySQL sees the status change CONFIRMED -> CANCELLED and fires the trigger.")
w("  Java code does NOT explicitly refund the payment. The trigger handles it.")
w("  PaymentDAO.updateRefunded() exists in the code but is not used for cancellation.")
w("")
w("---")
w("")
w("## Seed Data Summary")
w("")
